      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Another update:\n\nI implemented a fix that repositions the two behind-the-head features in Hokyl Night to be closer together so they can function in the new system, but this closer positioning also tends to interfere with players grabbing other items which are close to their head and spams controller haptics especially when in motion.\n\nSpecifically: the change reduces the available margin of error which is normally used to make head-following-features more resilient to varying avatar configurations and more robust against floating point precision loss at distance.\n\nThe result is a reduction in reliability or an increase in (costly, less-performant) script complexity to counter it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
